# FLOQR package versions

Format: `{channel}{major}.{minor}.{patch}` — example `s3.0.0`.

## Page links never carry a version (owner decision Oct 10 2026, s3.1.37)

- **No `v=` on any page / navigation / shareable link** — static `<a href>`, hub / menu / Back links, FloqAi links, Venue Links, club-embed, Inbox / email / SMS notification links built by Functions, `returnTo`, sign-in redirects (`loginHref`, `profile-access-guard.js`), portal iframe `src` (keep `embed=1`, no `v`).
- Old URLs that still have `?v=` keep working: the value is ignored and never propagated (`FLOQRNav.buildUrl` / `stampCurrentVersion` delete it, `safeReturnTo` / `returnPath` drop it).
- **Only asset tags** (`<script src>`, `<link href>`, image tags) carry `?v=<package>` for cache-busting, and **only the bump script** writes them — every asset tag is re-stamped to the current package on each release.
- `FLOQRNav.appVersion` is the asset / package id only. Never use it to build a page link.
- Xibo Display URLs (`display.html?location=` / `display2.html?location=`) never get `?v=` or `?screen=`.

## Channels

| Prefix | Name | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| **s** | **Stable** | Production-ready major line. Current line is **s3**. |
| **r** | Standard release | Optional label for a minor inside the stable line (`s3.1.0` is enough; do not invent a second number). |
| **h** | Hotfix | Emergency patch on the current stable (`s3.0.1`). |
| **d** | Development | Workspace-only experiments. Do not publish Pages as `d*`. |

Retired: `v29.09.N`. Treat those strings as historical cache keys only.

## What to bump

- **Major (`s3` → `s4`)** — breaking public API / DTO, named “major release”, or a new stable product line.
- **Minor (`s3.1.0`)** — new user-visible feature that stays compatible.
- **Patch (`s3.0.1`)** — fix, copy, help, diagnostics, CSS.

This workspace’s current stable is **s3.1.37**.

